<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB, Sulzer get guarantees on Three Gorges.</title>
<headline>ABB, Sulzer get guarantees on Three Gorges.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss government has agreed in principle to grant export credit guarantees for ABB Asea Brown Boveri and Sulzer AG for work on China's Three Gorges dam project, the Economics Ministry said.</p>
<p>ABB's Swiss unit leads an international consortium of ABB companies seeking to provide 14 generators for the huge project, which has drawn fire from environmentalist groups.</p>
<p>ABB's total offer is worth 700 million Swiss francs. Around half the work would come to Switzerland.</p>
<p>Sulzer wants to deliver turbine components worth 25 million francs.</p>
<p>Companies wishing to take part in a international tender on the project are required to obtain project financing guarantees.</p>
<p>The project consists of two power plants with an installed capacity of 18,200 megawatts, a flood relief system, and locks for navigation.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
